  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adult education for concientous local citizen participation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Whilst levels of community organisation in El Salvador and throughout Central America are relatively good, grassroots sectors of civil society are often lacking basic information, analysis and understanding about the economic and political systems, structures and trends that shape their reality and impact their lives and livelihoods. There are very few spaces for systematic training of grassroots and community leaders and educators (agents of change) in education, analysis and reflection and a scarcity of publishing houses dedicated to producing quality, digestible educational support materials on social, economic, political and environmental development issues for these popular sectors. Equipo Ma&#xED;z is dedicated to adult (popular) education through publications and training and aims to facilitate learning and analysis at the grassroots on issues that affect local people to enable them to have a better understanding of these issues and the capacity to propose alternative policies. It aims to increase people&#x2019;s commitment to social justice and encourage them to take an active role in creating change.   Through this project Equipo Ma&#xED;z will provide training for over 1,605 agents of social change, as well as producing new and re-editing existing publications and materials. Of special interest in this new cycle are reflections on doing grass roots work within one&apos;s organization and developing useful tools for this. The application of practical and strategic gender approaches in all aspects of MAIZ&apos;s operational and programmatic work is noteworthy, something which is being continued and strengthened in this new proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
